## 📂 Project Structure

The repository is organized topic-wise under the src directory.


> The folder names above reflect the current repository structure. As the repository evolves, folder names may be cleaned up to follow consistent Python naming conventions.

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/avinash4tripathi/Python.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the Repository

```bash
cd Python
```

### 3. Verify Python Installation

```bash
python --version
```

Example:

```text
Python 3.14.0
```

### 4. Create a Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

### 5. Activate the Virtual Environment

#### Windows

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

#### macOS / Linux

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

### 6. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 7. Run a Python Program

Navigate to the required topic and run:

```bash
python filename.py
```

---

## 🌱 Virtual Environment

This project can be developed inside a Python virtual environment to keep dependencies isolated.

Create:

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate:

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

Check installed packages:

```bash
pip list
```

Deactivate:

```bash
deactivate
```

> The `venv/` directory should generally not be committed to GitHub. Add it to `.gitignore`.

---

## 📦 Package Management

### View Installed Packages

```bash
pip list
```

### Install a Package

```bash
pip install package_name
```

### Update a Package

```bash
pip install --upgrade package_name
```

### Uninstall a Package

```bash
pip uninstall package_name
```

### Generate `requirements.txt`

```bash
pip freeze > requirements.txt
```

### Install From `requirements.txt`

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

